findings.description:
The initiative plan puts "GPU-accelerated force accumulation (CuPy/CUDA) and multi-resolution simulation strategies (variable-rate ticking, agent aggregation)" in initiative 620 (`001-initiative-plan.migratory.md:62-66`). This doc nonetheless:
- lists "Aggregation interface support" as one of its own Anticipated Slices (line 115);
- spends two of eight Technical Considerations (lines 97, 99) on the 500K–4M tiers;
- imposes GPU-driven constraints ("no dynamic allocation") on today's CPU hot loop.

Meanwhile it has no slice for swarm, which the plan *does* assign here, and none for migration, which line 19 names as an engine output. Cut the aggregation slice and the GPU section down to one line: the interface must stay array-in/array-out, and the details are in 620. Use the space for the archetypes this initiative actually owns.
